WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very well, thanks.
How are you?

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.403
-Good.
I'm very happy to have you here.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're big fans
of "The Crown" here,

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we kind of completed
the trifecta,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.376
because we had Matt Smith here,
who was Prince Philip.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.312
We had Vanessa Kirby, who was
Margaret, and now we have you.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we're very -- very happy
to complete the set.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The whole set.
-The whole set.

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:16.950 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Whole set of royals.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now you are not in
the next season of "The Crown"

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you're being replaced
by Olivia Colman,

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is another
fantastic actress.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you take anything
when you left?

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seemed like that's
a set where --

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.728 line:92%
a lot of good stuff to steal.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.964 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, there'd be loads
of good stuff to steal,

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.600
but they keep it under ---
they keep it under lock and key.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they need it all,
as well.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they'd know who'd taken it.
It would be pretty obvious.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, that's true.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
When one cast leaves
and another one comes in,

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have a lot of suspects.
-I deny everything.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I have nothing.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:44.411 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Do you miss it?

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you miss playing someone
of that stature?

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.215
It must have been nice to be
called Queen all the time.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.884 line:92%
-No one ever called me Queen.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:52.752
-Yeah, I guess that's a good
point as I'm thinking about it.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Walked over, "Hello, Queen."
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, Queen,
we got trouble again."

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.427 line:92%
-"Nice to see you today, Queen."

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.661 line:92%
That'd be great if they did.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they should have
done that.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.231
-Yeah. No. They never did.
They never called me Queen.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:09.869
But I don't miss the stature of
the part, but I miss the people.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:13.073
-Yeah. I imagine it's very hard
to leave a show like that.

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:16.009
I will say, you know, any actor
would have a fear of,

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:18.511
"Oh, I hope I don't get typecast
in roles like this."

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.213
You've certainly shook that off
right away

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:25.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
by going from the Queen to
Lisbeth Salander in this film.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:29.355
Or it makes me look like I've
got psychological problems.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:29.856 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:30.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, I hadn't even
thought of that.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:32.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right.
So, it might be that, as well.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:37.730
But definitely far more leather
in "Girl With --"

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
Far more leather
and I'm thinking more tattoos

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
than "The Crown."

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.204 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I mean, I don't know.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.640
You never know what goes on from
the neck down with the Queen.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.208 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.642 size:78% position:39%
-She could be hiding
an awful lot of tats.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would be a fun thing
to find out.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wouldn't it?
-Yeah.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.314 line:92%
-How could we find that out?

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:54.881 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't know.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:58.485
I guess -- I guess the reality
is, if you haven't found it out,

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
none of us
are going to find it out.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.454
'Cause you probably did
more research than I did,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and if you never came across
the tattoo part.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.525 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I hope so.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.659 line:92%
-But I would think the Queen,

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
if the Queen had a bunch
of tattoos --

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.663
and again, this is just me
blue-skying and dreaming.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.933
-Okay, let's do this.
-I wish it was some kind of map.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.903 line:92%
-Over her whole body or --

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, like,
just every part of her

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:19.939 line:92%
that you can't see in clothes,

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.742
there's, like, some sort of map
that's very key to the --

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like a treasure map?
-Yeah.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:28.781
I mean, she's a queen and so,
you know, they put it on her.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
When's it okay to --

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, no.
She's a royal.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it might not
have been up to her.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.189 line:92%
They might have been like,

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Let's get this map
on this baby, pronto."

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
Again, I don't know
if this is true or not.

00:02:40.527 --> 00:02:44.164
-I'd much prefer if she had,
like, Prince Philip on one arm,

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.832 size:78% position:39% line:92%
a corgi on the other.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A corgi, yeah.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.967 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Her handbag just --

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but, like,
not just a corgi.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.538 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Like, corgi for life.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.305 line:92%
-All the corgis she's had.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
She'd have a sleeve
of all the corgis she'd had.

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right cause they don't --
I mean, this is a spoiler,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
but all those corgis haven't
lived as long as she has.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's gone through
a bunch of them.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
She's gone through loads.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's gone through loads
of corgis.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:04.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, there's a really high
corgi turnover.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
They say, you know,
when you're a corgi

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.655
and, you know, you're at the --
They go, "Oh, my God.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.455 line:92%
This is life of the corgi."

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they go, "Yeah,
we don't last that long."

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.594 line:92%
-Was it fun to -- Lisbeth --

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:17.897
Obviously this is a continuation
of this story.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.600
Was that -- Were these books --
books you were familiar with?

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, I'd read --
I hadn't read the fourth book.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hadn't read
"Girl in the Spider's Web."

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:29.142
I'd read the "Millennium" series
when they first came out.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And more -- far more fighting
than "The Crown,"

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot more stunts.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.449
-It was my only criticism of you
in "The Crown."

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were almost no stunts
and fights.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
Yeah, I didn't do any.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:42.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You didn't do any stunts?
Did you do stunts in this one?

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And did you enjoy it?

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it something you thought
was important?

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you think
it would be thrilling?

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wouldn't say
it was thrilling.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.265
I mean, you sort of try and
approach it as a professional

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not going,
"Yeah, I'm bloodthirsty.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't wait to fake-punch
people in the face."

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.003 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But there is an element
that's quite fun.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I would only imagine.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.243 line:92%
Plus you're working with people

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:06.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are excellent
at not hurting you.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:06.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say, like,
if you're a stunt person

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose job is to fight you
in that film,

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:13.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
they really have
a hands-off policy, probably.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
They know what they're doing.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, whereas you're probably
just throwing roundhouses

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hitting them.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:19.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Left and right.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just, you know,
uppercuts and all sorts.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:27.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was filmed in Stockholm
and Berlin in the winter.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.001 line:92%
Those are wonderful cities.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've never been there
in the winter.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:34.474 line:92%
They seem very cold and gray.

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:35.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.076 line:92%
-I mean, cold more than gray.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have some beautiful,
crisp mornings.

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:44.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, like subzero,
like, freezing, freezing cold.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, you know,
there are a lot of --

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
See, I mean, again,
a lot of leather,

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of helmets,
a lot of motorcycles.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.425
I would imagine, I mean, you're
not riding the motorcycles,

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.727
but you were not in a lot
of parkas in this film.

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.929 line:92%
-You must have been cold a lot.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.599
-I was cold a lot there.
I definitely vary in size.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:02.235
I tried to put as many
thermal layers underneath

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.136 size:75% position:38% line:92%
as humanly possible,

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
so sometimes I'm a bit
like a sausage

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:08.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
and some of my leather outfits
are bursting at the seams.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are scenes
where you can tell

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.645
you can't really move your arm,
yeah.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like,
"We got to go over here."

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.516 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-But -- But yeah.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:24.490
-How would you even describe
the hairstyle of the character?

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:28.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was mainly a bowl cut
on top,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then underneath
it was shaved.

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a bit of a fringe.
I like to mix it up.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes it was a Mohawk.
-Yeah.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
There we kind of looked at,
like, similar haircuts

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:39.238
that had that sort of Mohawk-y,
fauxhawk-y feeling.

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:41.274 line:92%
-Very similar to Rihanna.

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:44.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, then we got --
-Yeah, and Tilda.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then this is Pink
with a little --

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's, like,
a pointy fauxhawk.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.550
-That was quite -- Yeah.
There's more on the sides.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And then there's that.

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the one.
-Yeah, that's the one.

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:55.822
-That's almost identical.
-I feel like it was, maybe.

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then people do always say,
"Oh, my God.

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would make
a great Lisbeth Salander,"

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:00.960 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to me all the time.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was happy for you
that you got it.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:04.864 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I was happy for you.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.666 size:75% position:38%
-That's really kind,
'cause I first said,

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:09.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Are sure you don't want Seth
to do it?"

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:09.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's so kind.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a feeling
you were a nice person.

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:13.439 line:92%
So thank you saying for that.

